  "notes": [
    "The RariFundController deployment immutably hard-linked AlphaPoolController 0xed2cd60c0000a990a5ffaf0e7ddc70a37d7c623f; both runtimes remained unchanged through the incident.",
    "Measured onchain as campaign net proceeds before gas. Immediately after the attacker's nonce-7 setup transaction, the EOA and helper jointly hold 1,040.677867052043994188 ETH; after the final successful nonce-191 transaction they hold 4,005.135463694322340589 ETH. Their increase is 2,964.457596642278346401 ETH, and the 184 consecutive successful campaign transactions at nonces 8 through 191 dispose of 23.17274534 ETH as gas. A separate non-campaign transaction sends 2 ETH from 0x0eb791bb0a62baffb28d46dfecfc650b4b82a16c to the EOA during the window, so net exploit proceeds before gas are 2,985.630341982278346401 ETH. Transfers between the two attacker-controlled accounts cancel. This account-based net measure is used because the transient ibETH manipulation makes a simple Rari/Alpha contract-balance delta overstate victim depletion. Rari's contemporaneous post-mortem rounded the extraction to about 2,600 ETH and $10 million."
